In the VSλ model, DAN firing rates begin to exhibit RPE signals. A sudden increase in positive reinforcements, for example at trial 20 in Fig. 2d, results in a sudden increase in d+, which then decays as the excitatory feedback from M− diminishes as a result of synaptic depression in w− (Fig. 2c–e). Similarly, sudden decrements in positive reinforcements, for example at trial 80, are signalled by reductions in d+. However, when the reinforcement magnitude exceeds the upper bound, as in trials 40–60 and 120–140 in Fig. 2, D± exhibits sustained elevations in firing rate from baseline by an amount \documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
