Responses in single DANs to the unconditioned stimulus (US), when paired with a CS+, should decay towards a baseline over successive CS ± US pairings, as a result of the learned changes in MBON firing rates. To the best of our knowledge, only one study has measured DAN responses throughout several CS–US pairings in Drosophila50. Consistent with DAN responses in our model, Dylla et al.50 reported such decaying responses in DANs in the γ- and \documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
